{"full":"hf:pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit","spaceId":"pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit","name":"MiniMax-H3 360° Orbit LoRA","source":"huggingface","description":"One photo into a frozen-instant 360° camera orbit","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":25,"created":"2026-09-28T11:36:43.000Z","updated":"2026-09-28T11:58:26.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://pablodawson-minimax-h3-360-orbit.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.363Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.363Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.363Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🌀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pablodawson/MiniMax-H3-360-Orbit-LoRA is a rank-16 ai-toolkit adapter for MiniMax-H3's first–last-frame (fl2va) partition that turns one photo into a frozen-time 360° camera orbit: the camera travels all the way around the subject, nothing in the scene moves, and the clip closes on the exact frame it started from — so orbits chain or stitch into longer shots with no visible seam.","Upload a photo and press Orbit 360°. The photo is fed to MiniMax-H3 as both the first and the last keyframe — the wiring the LoRA was trained with, and what pins both ends. Every knob the card recommends is preset: 768×768, 73 frames (≈ 3 s at 24 fps), 28 steps, no CFG (MiniMax-H3 is guidance-distilled, so there is no negative prompt either), adapter strength 1.0, audio off, and the frozen-instant prompt used verbatim as the training captions had it:","One frozen instant. Only the camera moves. In a continuous 360 orbit. Preserve every person and object in exactly the same world position, orientation, shape and pose throughout the shot. Airborne objects remain suspended at the captured height and angle: no wobbling, shaking, spinning, drifting, falling or continued action. Keep faces, hands, clothing, liquids and the background motionless while retaining their natural appearance. Camera parallax is the only source of apparent movement. No cuts, zoom, morphing or added objects."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"473f1559fd83c84863de3ac98f4a92e64f86d9d4093090611ae27f82a3014916","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.439Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.439Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"pablodawson/MiniMax-H3-360-Orbit-LoRA is a rank-16 ai-toolkit adapter for MiniMax-H3's first–last-frame (fl2va) partition that turns one photo into a frozen-time 360° camera orbit: the camera travels all the way around the subject, nothing in the scene moves, and the clip closes on the exact frame it started from — so orbits chain or stitch into longer shots with no visible seam.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"473f1559fd83c84863de3ac98f4a92e64f86d9d4093090611ae27f82a3014916","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.439Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-28T11:58:26.000Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/pablodawson/minimax-h3-360-orbit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T09:39:53.439Z","hash":"473f1559fd83c84863de3ac98f4a92e64f86d9d4093090611ae27f82a3014916","originalBytes":9294,"storedBytes":9294,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["lora","space","conditioner","adapter","minimax-h3","same","every","frames","card","first","orbit","request","both","camera","gradio","one","photo","proj","run","token","two","weights","against","audio","base","default","diffusers","example","gpu","multimodalart","only","prompt","pruned","rather","strength","under","which","between